[Music]  hey guys it's Jonah here so I'm going to  take you in the gym and we'll be doing  my favorite fat burning team circuit  training there will be three separate  stations strength cardio and core so for  each station we will be doing five  different exercises in five minutes and  we want to repeat all the stations twice  so the total workout time will be about  a forty minutes let's start on the  strength station and work on our total  body  the first exercise will be lunge and  twist so this workout works on the legs  hips and the twisting motion will work  on your core and obliques so grab a ball  or a kettlebell that weighs between four  to eight kilos if you're an absolute  beginner you can perform this workout  without any weight as you lunge forward  or with check that both legs are hip  width apart and point it forward as you  lower yourself your legs should be at a  90 degree angle then engage your core  extend your arms forward and twist to  the opposite side so we want to perform  each workout for 50 seconds with a quick  10 seconds transition in between the  next workout will be burpees press up  which works more on your upper body  chest and showed it again you can use a  ball or a capybara with between four to  eight kilos start standing tall as you  lower yourself place the weight on the  floor jump both legs back and lower  yourself into a push-up position  then jump back in and as you rise up to  stand press the weight overhead repeat  as many reps as you can in 50 seconds  when you're in a push-up position always  make sure that your back is flat and  core engaged as depress the with  overhead avoid arching your lower back  now let's bring our heart rate back up  the third workout is stepper squat jump  you can also do this workout using a big  box squats and hop on to the stepper and  hop back down when you land it is very  important to keep your knees soft and  land in a squat position  so never lock your knees  or land extending this word God will  really push your hunter it up and you  will really feel the burn in your size  and come this next workout is really fun  ball slams this will develop power  strength speed and coordination grab a  wicked med ball and stand in a white  stump  bring the ball overhead contract your  abs bend your knees and drag the chest  down to slam the ball into the ground  with as much force as possible retrieve  the ball as it bounces up and  immediately go into your neck strap  perform this exercise with maximum  effort and remember to keep your knees  bent push your butt back as you slam the  ball this exercise works the entire body  and it burns crazy amounts of calories  for the final workout in the strength  station let's work on our back muscles  back row you can do this workout with a  barbell a pair of dumbbells or fitness  bag just like what I have here so stand  sugar with the pot keep your knees soft  and bend forward at your hips until your  total is nearly parallel to the floor  pull the fitness bag or barbell up to  with your belly keep your elbows pointed  back chest up and back slaps squeeze  your back muscles for a second or two  right at the top and lower yourself to  starting position  perform as many repetitions as you can  within one minute rest you're done with  the strength station that was five  minutes long now take a one-minute break  breathe keep yourself hydrated and we  want to move on to the cardio station  let's hit the treadmill for the next  five minutes if you were to go for a  low-impact workout you can also choose  to use a bike cross trainer or even  stepper in order to maximize fat burn we  want to play around with the speed so on  the first third and final minute I want  you to sprint as fast as you can between  11 and 13 kilometers per hour remember  to pace a breathing to help you run  faster and longer  feel the burn feel your heart rate  pumping and stay strong so between the  second and fourth minutes I want you to  bring the spit down to either a slow jog  or walk and recover take this minute to  really catch your breath breathe deeply  and bring your heart rate down slightly  if you struggle remember to focus on  your goal and run with your heart okay  well done that was five minutes of speed  interval training on the cardio station  now take a one-minute break and we want  to move on to the final station core the  first exercise will be full extension to  work on your upper and lower abs you can  use a weighted ball  dumbbells plates or kettlebell hold the  ball with both hands and lie on your  back with your arms extended overhead  and legs straight out as you breathe out  go up and bring your knees to your chest  and your arms towards your legs keep  your core tight and slowly return to  starting position avoid arching your  lower back your legs should only go down  as far as you can while keeping your  back flat again we want to do as many  repetitions as we can in 50 seconds  without sacrificing to perform next my  favourite core workout by the man plank  to challenge yourself place both hands  on the ball and perform the exercise  keep your back flat and bring one knee  towards your elbow really engage your  core to keep your balance if this is too  tough for you then do without the ball  and keep your palms on the mat this is a  great core workout and you will also  feel it in your arms and showed it the  third exercise is Russian twist which  works on the entire core and also  obliques so hold a ball cut the bell or  dumbbells directly in front of you sit  on the mat with your knees bent and feet  flat on the floor then keeping the spine  long lean back slightly until you feel  your core engaged beginners you can  place both feet on the floor to  challenge yourself lift both legs a few  inches of the floor and keep twisting  perform this exercise in a smooth  continuous motion so don't let the  weight rest on the floor  let's lie on your back and perform  flutter kicks this is a killer workout  for your lower abs you can place both  hands it's just by your ears and lift  your shoulders few inches of the floor  without tensing your neck lift both feet  off the ground and move your legs in a  fluttering up and down motion keep the  movement small to really work on your  lower abs beginners you can rest your  head on the mat and take your arms by  your sides  choose under your butt to support your  lower back keep your abs constantly  contracted throughout the exercise so  going for your breath okay breathe as  you move your legs now let's bring our  heart rate back up as we enter the  course station let's hit it with  mountain climber start in a high plank  position with the hands slightly wider  they should width apart and get your  core and drive your knee up to with your  chest one at a time while maintaining  your body as straight as possible keep  the movement as far as you can and bring  your heart rate up to challenge yourself  even more but if your arms on a ball it  is not easy but this is a great  progression to really improve on your  balance keep pushing yourself  don't stop now because this is the final  workout and rest relax wind down and get  into a child's pose breathe and just  bring your heart rate down take between  one to two minutes break and we want to  repeat all three stations for another  round this is my favorite jeans circuit  training which I like to do twice weekly  it combines strength cardio and of the  core so the goal is to take short breaks  to constantly keep your heart rate  elevated and as a result you'll be  burning a lot more calories as you  progress you can also mix and measure  the workouts so the next time you hit  the gym try this to give this video a  thumbs up share it and subscribe to my  youtube channel for a lot more new  videos every week you also turn on your  notification button so that you will get  notified every time I upload a new  video all the best

